COPYLEFT: NONE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

There is no copyleft dependency in any Go module or in the JavaScript
tree.

github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum (LGPL-3.0) was one, imported by nine
files across four modules. It has been removed, and CI fails any module
that reintroduces it -- `go mod why` per module, which catches a
transitive path as well as a direct import.

That matters commercially rather than technically: the LGPL obliges
whoever receives a distributed binary to be able to relink it against
their own build of the library, and Go links statically. Shipping source
discharged it; shipping images would not have.

See docs/engineering/GO-ETHEREUM-REMOVAL.md.

